# Hyphens, not long dashes

In user-facing text (articles, UI copy, metadata, comments shown to users), use a regular hyphen `-` only.

- Do **not** use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`)
- Use `-` for asides, ranges, list separators, and source attributions

```text
❌ Work in progress — hymn lists…
✅ Work in progress - hymn lists…

❌ (1960–1962)
✅ (1960-1962)

❌ Qaltha — Page ܢܕ — Aykan Masya
✅ Qaltha - Page ܢܕ - Aykan Masya
```
